The fork's second change to SDL3 3.4.16: SDL_GPU's Direct3D 12 backend keeps its descriptor writes inside
their heaps.

Why: D3D12_INTERNAL_WriteGPUDescriptors switched to new shader-visible heaps only when the current one was
already full (index >= max), then wrote the whole table ("FIXME: need to error on overflow"). A table that
did not fit ran past the heap's end: the 2048-slot sampler heap at 2046 + 4, then D3D12 EXECUTION ERROR 646
under the debug layer, and memory corruption or a lost device on WARP, where the heap is process memory
(the -d3d12 renderer's crashes on Windows ARM64). A switch between two tables of one draw also left the
tables written before it pointing into the old heaps, which SetDescriptorHeaps makes undefined.

What changes:
- BindGraphicsResources and BindComputeResources count the descriptors the bind will write and switch
  heaps before writing any of it when they do not fit (EnsureGPUDescriptorSpace). After any switch every
  descriptor table is marked to be written again, the compute read-write tables included (moved into a
  helper so they can be).
- WriteGPUDescriptors keeps its switch as a last line (index + count > max): it keeps the write inside a
  heap and refuses that draw or dispatch.
- A heap the pool could not make is no longer used unchecked: the draw or dispatch is refused instead.
- Each guard logs once, loudly (SDL_LogError, GPU category), and is counted. The counts, with the heaps
  made, the most out at once, the most held by one command buffer and the heap switches, are printed when
  the device is destroyed: always if a guard fired, otherwise with ZH_SDL_GPU_D3D12_STATS=1, which also
  prints each new most of 8, 16, 32 ... as it happens (heaps out, heaps held by one command buffer, command
  buffers submitted and not yet cleaned). A correct run shows 0 late switches, 0 heap failures, 0 refused
  draws and 0 refused dispatches.
- Two fixes from upstream SDL main, as they are there: 67bf94eed5 (RegisterMessageCallback is given a
  cookie; with NULL it fails with E_INVALIDARG and the debug layer's messages never reach SDL's log) and
  f443c429c6 (SubmitAndAcquireFence reads the fence while submitLock is held).

Two hunks are upstream SDL's own changes, backported unchanged from SDL's main branch: 67bf94eed5
(RegisterMessageCallback is given a cookie) and f443c429c6 (SubmitAndAcquireFence reads the fence while
submitLock is held); every other added line is this port's and is marked.

Every run where the old code did not overflow is unchanged, except that a command buffer's first heaps
now also mark its tables for a rebind (a few descriptor copies once per command buffer).

Upstream (checked 2026-09-29): SDL main has the same WriteGPUDescriptors, FIXME included; 67bf94eed5 and
f443c429c6 are there and are not in any 3.4 release.

Remove when: this tree moves to an SDL release whose D3D12 backend makes room before it writes a table (or
errors on overflow) and carries the two upstream fixes. Applied by Tools/vendor.ps1 -D3D12 and
Tools/vendor.sh; CMakeLists.txt refuses a ZH_D3D12 build of a tree without it.

